    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/operations-manager/job/P1-6661605-0": {
      "title": "Site Navigation",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Operations Manager Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Operations Manager Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-026097 Share this Job 4001 South 700 East, Salt Lake City UT, United States Posting Date: 09/08/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $68,300.00 - $102,500.00 Work Location This is a full-time, in-office role based in our Salt Lake City, Utah office. Make an Impact at WGU As an Operations Manager, you'll oversee and lead established operational functions across multiple business units. You'll partner with leaders across the university to figure out what needs fixing, prioritize the initiatives that will move the needle, and drive them from idea to execution. This role is a good mix of big-picture thinking and hands-on delivery — you'll help set standards based on best practices, dig into data to see what's working and what isn't, and lead the cross-functional work needed to actually make improvements stick. Everything comes back to one goal: making things run better for our learners and our employees. What You'll Do Partner with initiative leaders — business partners, project managers, business owners, and others — to deliver operational services, programs, and initiatives Work with leadership to define process improvement strategies, both short- and long-term, that are scalable and support continuous improvement Analyze current business operations, processes, and systems to spot opportunities for improvement Establish key operational metrics, analyze the data, and use it to shape improvement initiatives Develop functional and department standards and policies in partnership with leaders and stakeholders Identify and implement solutions that improve operations and support functional and department goals Lead cross-functional teams to put new standards and business models into practice across the department Determine the best use of available resources and build efficient partnerships across functional operations Build and lead communication and training plans for anyone impacted by process changes or operational improvements Keep an eye on new trends and technologies that could support current or future operational needs Set up audits and reporting to keep data accurate and reliable Take on other related duties as they come up What You'll Bring Ability to plan, organize, coordinate, and lead projects in a way that ties back to bigger strategic goals Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills Clear, effective communication skills, both written and verbal Strong organizational skills and a genuine attention to detail Ability to build consensus and keep people motivated Comfort creating and tracking data tied to project impact A track record of coaching others and giving useful feedback Strong listening skills and the ability to adapt well when things change Ability to look at business operations and processes and identify where things can improve Broad management know-how, with deep expertise in your own area and an understanding of how your work affects the rest of the university What You'll Bring — Qualifications Bachelor's degree in a related field of study Two or more years of related work experience, including experience with project management and change management Bonus Points PMP or CMP certification Change Practitioner certification Six Sigma certification Master's degree in a related field of study Experience in Lieu of Education Equivalent relevant experience performing the essential functions of this role may substitute for education requirements. Generally, one year of relevant experience may be considered in place of one year of education, at the discretion of the hiring manager. Physical Requirements Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer Must be able to lift up to 15 pounds at times What to Expect At WGU, our mission drives everything we do, including how we hire. Our interview experience is designed to give qualified candidates the opportunity to demonstrate their experience through meaningful conversations and collaboration. We thoughtfully review every application and invite forward candidates whose experience and potential best align with the role and our mission. Interview Steps: Introductory call Hiring manager interview Additional interview Visa Sponsorship While we welcome applicants from all backgrounds, WGU is not able to provide visa sponsorship for this role. Travel Expectation This position requires occasional travel of up to 20%, including required attendance at designated company summits (typically one to two per year). Additional travel may include conferences, visits to company locations, and other business-related events as needed. Additional Information Full-Time Regular Positions (classified as regular and working 40 standard weekly hours): This is a full-time, regular position (classified for 40 standard weekly hours) that is eligible for bonuses; medical, dental, vision, telehealth and mental healthcare; health savings account and flexible spending account; basic and voluntary life insurance; disability coverage; accident, critical illness and hospital indemnity supplemental coverages; legal and identity theft coverage; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; discounted WGU tuition; and flexible paid time off for rest and relaxation with no need for accrual, flexible paid sick time with no need for accrual, 11 paid holidays, and other paid leaves, including up to 12 weeks of parental leave. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/senior-strategist-future-of-education-and-ai-innovation/job/P1-6663477-0": {
      "title": "Site Navigation",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Senior Strategist - Future of Education and AI Innovation Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Senior Strategist - Future of Education and AI Innovation Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-026100 Share this Job 4001 South 700 East, Salt Lake City UT, United States Posting Date: 09/04/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $109,900.00 - $170,400.00 Location: This position will be based on-site at our Salt Lake City, UT office. Essential Functions and Responsibilities Innovation Portfolio Ownership : Own a portfolio of Innovation initiatives end-to-end, from problem framing and hypothesis through prototype, evaluation, and handoff or sunset. Recommend which initiatives advance, scale, or stop. Strategy Development : Develop AI strategies that connect emerging capabilities to specific student outcomes and institutional priorities. Translate broad direction from leadership into scoped, testable workstreams. Prototyping and Experimentation : Design and build prototypes and experiments that test whether an approach works before the university invests in it. Define the question, the method, and the threshold for success in advance. Evidence and Evaluation Design : Set the evaluation design for assigned initiatives, including instrumentation, measures, comparison conditions, and analysis plan. Produce findings that partners can act on and defend. Data Analysis and Insight : Analyze quantitative and qualitative data to produce insights that change decisions. Distinguish signal from noise and state confidence honestly. Cross-Functional Partnership : Build durable working relationships with academic programs, assessment, technology, institutional research, and student-facing operations. Secure the alignment an initiative needs before it needs it. Responsible AI Practice : Apply the university’s Responsible AI standards throughout design and deployment. Identify ethical, legal, privacy, accessibility, and bias risks early, document them, and drive mitigation with the AI Ethicist and governance partners. Emerging Technology Assessment : Track the AI and learning technology landscape. Evaluate vendors, models, tools, and research, and convert what matters into clear recommendations with tradeoffs and cost. Knowledge Transfer and Enablement : Build the artifacts that let others use the work, including documentation, playbooks, briefings, and training. Mentorship : Provide guidance, review, and feedback to Strategists. Raise the quality of the team’s methods and output. Communication : Present complex technical work to non-technical audiences, including executive leadership and external partners, in plain language with the substance intact. Performs other related duties as assigned. Senior Level Duties Lead assigned initiatives with minimal direction, setting scope, method, and sequence within strategic priorities established by leadership. Serve as the team’s subject matter expert on one or more AI domains and act as the primary point of contact for partner teams in those domains. Represent Program Experience Futures in cross-departmental working groups and governance forums. Identify and escalate risks, dependencies, and resource constraints before they affect delivery. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Deep understanding of AI and machine learning technologies, including current model capabilities, limitations, and failure modes. Working knowledge of synthetic data, evaluation methodology, and experimental design. Strong quantitative skills, including proficiency with data analysis tooling and the judgment to choose the right method for the question. Ability to frame ambiguous problems, define success criteria, and produce a plan others can follow. Fluency in the ethical, legal, privacy, and accessibility considerations that govern AI in education. Excellent written communication. Ability to produce documents that survive executive scrutiny. Strong interpersonal skills and credibility with technical and academic audiences alike. Advanced project management skills, including the ability to run several concurrent initiatives at different stages. Comfort with uncertainty, rapid iteration, and work that may be discontinued based on evidence. Ability to mentor and elevate the work of less experienced colleagues. Minimum Qualifications 5+ years of related experience with a bachelor’s degree, or 3+ years with a master’s degree, or a Doctorate or Terminal degree, in Business Administration, Education, Computer Science, or related field. 4+ years of experience in strategic planning, product strategy, program management, or applied research within higher education or a similar industry. Demonstrated experience taking an AI or emerging technology initiative from concept through evaluated implementation. Proficiency in data analysis and use of relevant software tools. Strong project management skills and experience managing complex projects from initiation to completion. Department Specific Minimum Qualifications Demonstrated experience in developing and refining educational programs, courses, and curricula within the higher education sector. Understanding of accreditation standards, regulatory requirements, and industry best practices related to program development and institutional compliance. Proven ability to design and assess curriculum effectiveness, learning outcomes, and student engagement strategies, particularly within a Competency-based Education model. Experience with online learning platforms, learning management systems (LMS), and educational technologies used in online and hybrid learning environments. Knowledge of adult learning theories and principles, including instructional design methodologies tailored to adult learners in diverse academic settings. Ability to collaborate effectively with academic departments, faculty members, subject matter experts, and instructional designers to develop and deliver high-quality educational programs. Experience designing and running pilots or studies in a live academic environment, including instrumentation and measurement. Proficiency in data analysis and interpretation to inform program development decisions, assess program efficacy, and identify areas for continuous improvement. Clear and concise communication skills, with the ability to articulate program objectives, outcomes, and value propositions to internal and external stakeholders. Willingness to explore innovative approaches to program development, incorporate emerging technologies, and adapt to evolving trends and student needs in higher education. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree or higher in Business Administration, Education, Computer Science, Learning Science, or related field. Hands-on experience building with large language models, including prompting, evaluation, retrieval, or agentic workflows. Experience with assessment design, psychometrics, or learning analytics. Experience contributing to AI governance, ethics review, or responsible AI standards. Publication, conference presentation, or other public contribution in learning technology, AI, or assessment. Experience working with diverse student populations in online learning environments. Knowledge of accessibility standards and guidelines for digital learning materials. Physical Requirements Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Must be able to lift up to 15 pounds at times. Job Description Disclaimer: This position description provides the major duties/responsibilities, requirements, and working conditions for the position. It is intended to be an accurate reflection of the current position, however management reserves the right to revise or change as necessary to meet organizational needs. Other responsibilities may be assigned when circumstances require. This position requires occasional travel of up to 20%, including required attendance at designated company summits (typically one to two per year). Additional travel may include conferences, visits to company locations, and other business-related events as needed. Additional travel may be assigned as needed to support business requirements. #LI-SA1 Additional Information Full-Time Regular Positions (classified as regular and working 40 standard weekly hours): This is a full-time, regular position (classified for 40 standard weekly hours) that is eligible for bonuses; medical, dental, vision, telehealth and mental healthcare; health savings account and flexible spending account; basic and voluntary life insurance; disability coverage; accident, critical illness and hospital indemnity supplemental coverages; legal and identity theft coverage; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; discounted WGU tuition; and flexible paid time off for rest and relaxation with no need for accrual, flexible paid sick time with no need for accrual, 11 paid holidays, and other paid leaves, including up to 12 weeks of parental leave. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/senior-psychometrician/job/P1-6324414-0": {
      "title": "Site Navigation",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Senior Psychometrician Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Senior Psychometrician Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-025820 Share this Job 4001 South 700 East, Salt Lake City UT, United States Posting Date: 09/03/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $88,600.00 - $132,900.00 Job Summary The Senior Psychometrician assists other Psychometricians in providing services to the Program Development Department. This individual acts in a support role within the department, helping to provide expertise in the measurement and design of assessments. The Senior Psychometrician helps to ensure the accuracy and validity of assessments and gathers data that is instrumental to improving students' performance at WGU. Essential Functions and Responsibilities: Analyzes data from various types of assessments using a variety of statistical methods. Under the guidance of more senior psychometricians, performs statistical analyses required for score reporting and data interpretation. Under the guidance of more senior psychometricians, performs data analyses such as item analyses and reliability analyses. Under the guidance of more senior psychometricians, creates graphs, charts, tables, and dashboards based on statistical analyses. Performs other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skill and Abilities: Excellent interpersonal skills and communication skills within the team Strong time management skills Attention to detail in one's own work Ability to work well with a team, including following instructions and guidance of more senior team members. Ability to produce analyses quickly. Strong technical skills, including Microsoft Office, especially Excel, and capacity or experience with SAS, R, or other analytical or statistical packages. Experience with Tableau or Power BI for data visualization. Experience retrieving and manipulating data from databases using SQL, R, or Python. Competencies: Organizational or Student Impact: Supports program/course initiatives to improve Key Results. May actively contribute to initiatives at the university, college, or cluster level. Problem Solving & Decision Making: Resolves problems that require broad-based consideration of variables at the program/course level. Work is situational and highly complex, and difficulties faced require detailed information gathering and analysis at the program/course. Assists in completing tasks to achieve team deliverables. Communication & Influence: May communicates and collaborate with fellow faculty members within and across disciplines and practice. Attends professional conferences and association meetings focused on the faculty member’s discipline or practice area and engaged in discourse with fellow attendees. May contribute to WGU and college brand development. Leadership & Talent Management Model's best practices within specialty areas, produce measurable results. Establish coverage within and between teams to meet service level agreements. Implements workflows and optimizes team resources. Follows sound change management practices. Job Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Psychometrics, Psychological Measurement, Educational Psychology, or related field (e.g., Industrial/Organization Psychology) with an emphasis on quantitative methods or psychometrics One (1) year of experience in testing, research, or closely related fields such as statistics and data analysis Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in Higher Education Physical Requirements: Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Must be able to lift up to 15 pounds at times. This position requires occasional travel of up to 20%, including required attendance at designated company summits (typically one to two per year). Additional travel may include conferences, visits to company locations, and other business-related events as needed. Additional travel may be assigned as needed to support business requirements. #LI-TM1 Additional Information Full-Time Regular Positions (classified as regular and working 40 standard weekly hours): This is a full-time, regular position (classified for 40 standard weekly hours) that is eligible for bonuses; medical, dental, vision, telehealth and mental healthcare; health savings account and flexible spending account; basic and voluntary life insurance; disability coverage; accident, critical illness and hospital indemnity supplemental coverages; legal and identity theft coverage; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; discounted WGU tuition; and flexible paid time off for rest and relaxation with no need for accrual, flexible paid sick time with no need for accrual, 11 paid holidays, and other paid leaves, including up to 12 weeks of parental leave. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/full-time-student-records-specialist-on-site-wgu-campus-salt-lake-city-location/job/P1-6577269-0": {
      "title": "Full-Time Student Records Specialist",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Full-Time Student Records Specialist - On-Site WGU Campus - Salt Lake City Location Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Full-Time Student Records Specialist - On-Site WGU Campus - Salt Lake City Location Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-026008 Share this Job 4001 South 700 East, Salt Lake City UT, United States Posting Date: 09/03/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $19.37 - $28.07 Primary Responsibilities Receives and responsibly maintains student documentation. Demonstrates all core competencies. Applies university rules, regulations, and policies accurately and to the benefit of the student. Updates and maintains academic records with a high degree of accuracy and confidentiality. Understands and adheres to FERPA regulations. Works under the direction of the immediate supervisor/manager on daily assigned tasks both independently and in a team environment. Demonstrates strong cooperative skills with the ability to perform effectively in a team environment. Prioritizes essential job functions while utilizing numerous systems. Requires cross-functional coordination and/or collaboration with other university teams to complete tasks, research, and data reconciliation. Performs moderately complex data reconciliation regularly. Handles high-level escalations with professionalism, keeping leadership updated on team performance, issues, and outcomes to ensure continuous improvement. Maintains accurate, timely documentation of procedures and student interactions, ensuring all relevant teams are informed of updates in policies and processes. Continuously identifies and addresses barriers in processes, offering solution-focused recommendations that enhance both the student experience and operational efficiency. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Associate’s degree in a related field. Two (2) or more years of experience within a Records or Registrar’s Office, Student Services, or another related higher education role responsible for reviewing, validating, researching, and updating student academic records. Equivalent relevant experience may be substituted for the education requirement. Generally, one year of relevant experience may substitute for one year of education, at the hiring manager’s discretion. Experience performing moderately complex research and data reconciliation. Strong written communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Ability to prioritize essential job functions, meet deadlines, and manage multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite products and applications. Ability to maintain accuracy, confidentiality, and compliance with university policies and FERPA requirements. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field. Experience working with Student Information Systems (SIS). Experience working with Customer Relationship Management (CRM) software. This job description includes a general representation of job requirements rather than a comprehensive inventory of all required responsibilities or work activities. The contents of this document or related job requirements may change at any time with or without notice. This position requires occasional travel of up to 20%, including required attendance at designated company summits (typically one to two per year). Additional travel may include conferences, visits to company locations, and other business-related events as needed. Additional travel may be assigned as needed to support business requirements. Additional Information Full-Time Regular Positions (classified as regular and working 40 standard weekly hours): This is a full-time, regular position (classified for 40 standard weekly hours) that is eligible for bonuses; medical, dental, vision, telehealth and mental healthcare; health savings account and flexible spending account; basic and voluntary life insurance; disability coverage; accident, critical illness and hospital indemnity supplemental coverages; legal and identity theft coverage; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; discounted WGU tuition; and flexible paid time off for rest and relaxation with no need for accrual, flexible paid sick time with no need for accrual, 11 paid holidays, and other paid leaves, including up to 12 weeks of parental leave. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/onsite-instructor-prelicensure-clinical-houston-tx-full-time/job/P1-5821657-0": {
      "title": "Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Houston, TX - Full Time Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Houston, TX - Full Time Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-025338 Share this Job 901 Bagby Street, Houston TX, United States Posting Date: 09/03/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $80,700.00 - $121,000.00 Job Description ​ ***This is an ON-SITE position in the Houston, TX region *** Prelicensure Clinical Instructors are subject matter experts who teach and mentor students when engaged in experiential clinical course work; in a remote/onsite environment. This faculty position varies in the type, length, and intensity of instructional methods and is based upon student and facility needs. The Clinical Instructor works on a team to support an assigned group of students and offers specialized instruction on challenging experiential/clinical course work. Faculty interacts with students in both group and one-on-one settings. The Clinical Instructor ensures students are successful within their clinical placement setting as they oversee clinical learning. Essential Functions and Responsibilities: Act as a steward for carrying out WGU’s mission and strategic vision.  This faculty must: Demonstrate a high level of commitment, effectiveness, and consistency. Serves as a professional role model for students in communication, ethical comportment, and problem-solving. Provides expertise in an assigned content area and maintains current knowledge in their field. Demonstrates an understanding of, and participates in, the implementation of the philosophy and goals of the program. Fosters students learning through innovative teaching practices; to include how to perform duties in the clinical setting. Responds with urgency to meet student needs and communicates professionally and respectfully with students and all other members of the WGU community. Makes appropriate student referrals for remediation or other needs, utilizing WGU policies and procedures. Communicates with the student's assigned coach/preceptor as needed to discuss student progress and concerns. Provide final review and approval for student's clinical time. Offers proactive support and outreach to assigned students. Uses technology-based teaching and communication platforms to aid students in the development of competencies. Submits electronic clinical student evaluation form(s) after completion of clinical intensive. Collaborates with other professionals within the university to promote a positive, student-obsessed atmosphere. Responsible for responding with urgency to changing requirements, priorities, and short deadlines. Maintains a working knowledge and understanding of relevant state regulations. Conducts both in-person and/remote methods of student evaluation Knowledge, Skill and Abilities: Must be able to work well under stress and meet deadlines. Capacity for self-motivation and working independently. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Aptitude for learning innovative technology. Must comply with site specific orientation and onboarding requirements. Problem Solving Skills: Investigates appropriate resources and involves partners when appropriate; future-oriented; assesses what will help/hinder achieving goals; focuses on what is important. Interpersonal Skills: Deals with others in a considerate, respectful, and unbiased manner; approaches conflict proactively; solicits and shares feedback openly; listens with empathy and maintains composure. Accuracy: Draws on information garnered from careful cultivation of a broad knowledge of WGU’s goals and processes; investigates beyond assumptions. Adaptability: Course corrects behaviors and communication style to meet the needs of a wide range of situations; tackles obstacles appropriately; is comfortable with ambiguity. Reliability: Accountable to others; does what it takes to get the job done; actions are consistent with words; follows through on commitments; exhibits exceptional integrity. Attitude: Displays commitment to the organization and to personal growth; self-motivated and able to motivate and inspire others; asserts self appropriately to champion ideas; tells the truth in a direct and constructive manner. Initiative: Self-directs with a strong bias for action; leads the way in improvement of performance or processes; displays keen interest in students and organization. Competencies: Organizational or Student Impact: Accountable for decisions that impact individual students. Facilitates learning experiences that support student's attainment of knowledge and skills. Acts independently in executing teaching practice with specific guidance from senior faculty and program leaders. Problem Solving & Decision Making: Works on diverse matters of various levels of complexity. Receives general direction from their immediate supervisor or manager. Able to effectively utilize resources to address student concerns and inquiries. Supports students' needs to help them achieve course or program outcomes at the individual student level. Follows university and department established policies and best practices. Communication & Influence: Communicates with students as appropriate to support student questions and needs. Communicates with fellow faculty members as appropriate within and outside of the department. Expected to provide feedback regarding discipline and practice leadership. Leadership & Talent Management Considered a contributing and collegial team member. Adheres to learning and operational quality guidance and instruction Supports initiatives within specialty. Displays a positive attitude toward change and supports change management practices Job Qualifications: Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in nursing; Education is verified. Two years minimum Nursing experience Work history demonstrating continuous advancement and success in roles requiring creative problem solving and collaboration. Unencumbered RN license Active, unencumbered license in designated state State and federal legislative requirements and college accreditation requirements may apply to maintain the necessary credentialing for this role. Work history demonstrating continuous advancement and success in roles requiring creative problem solving and collaboration. As needed, support the Health Placement Team to secure clinical partnerships. This position requires occasional travel of up to 20%, including required attendance at designated company summits (typically one to two per year). Additional travel may include conferences, visits to company locations, and other business-related events as needed. Additional travel may be assigned as needed to support business requirements. Preferred: Doctorate, or terminal degree in a specific content area. Strong experience with distance education and distance learning students is preferred. Terminal degree and all applicable licenses or certifications. Prior experience in clinical teaching/nursing education. , support the Health Placement Team to secure clinical partnerships. Physical Requirements: Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Must be able to lift up to 15 pounds at times. Specific requirements of the job such as travel and the environment in which the job is performed. Additional Information Full-Time Regular Positions (classified as regular and working 40 standard weekly hours): This is a full-time, regular position (classified for 40 standard weekly hours) that is eligible for bonuses; medical, dental, vision, telehealth and mental healthcare; health savings account and flexible spending account; basic and voluntary life insurance; disability coverage; accident, critical illness and hospital indemnity supplemental coverages; legal and identity theft coverage; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; discounted WGU tuition; and flexible paid time off for rest and relaxation with no need for accrual, flexible paid sick time with no need for accrual, 11 paid holidays, and other paid leaves, including up to 12 weeks of parental leave. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/onsite-instructor-learning-lab-indianapolis-in-part-time/job/P1-6649440-0": {
      "title": "Onsite Instructor, Learning Lab",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Onsite Instructor, Learning Lab - Indianapolis, IN - Part Time Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Onsite Instructor, Learning Lab - Indianapolis, IN - Part Time Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-026079 Share this Job 9301 E 59th St, Indianapolis IN, United States Posting Date: 09/03/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $38.79 - $58.17 **This position is located ON-SITE in the WGU Clinical Learning & Simulation Center in Indianapolis, IN. Must have availability to work two (2) shifts per month during the hours of operation (Monday - Friday 7:30 am - 4:30 pm) as needed.** The Instructor, Learning Lab is a clinically experienced subject matter expert who is responsible for facilitating student learning and performance assessment(s) in on-site Clinical Learning Labs. Student learning activities in Clinical Learning Labs range from learning basic nursing skills to resolving simple-to-complex patient care situations via high-fidelity simulation. Teaching responsibilities can include traditional basic nursing skills and nursing care with high-fidelity simulation. Essential Functions and Responsibilities: Serves as a professional role model for students in dress, communication, deportment, problem solving, care delivery and patient advocacy to facilitate student’s socialization into the profession. Demonstrates understanding of and participates in implementation of the philosophy and goals of the nursing program. Demonstrates respect for the student as a new learner by communicating constructive feedback. Uses evidence-based tools and measures to evaluate the students’ clinical learning. Maintains communication with the Supervisor, Lab Faculty to make appropriate student referrals for remediation or other needs in post lab reports. Engages in teaching through demonstration, practice, and assistance. Facilitates student advancement through the performance of basic nursing skills to resolution of simple and/or complex patient care situations via high-fidelity simulation. When teaching in a simulated environment, the candidate demonstrates the ability to facilitate scenarios according to evidence-based standards and guidelines. Assists the student with application of clinical judgment, critical thinking, problem solving using reflection, probing, active listening, and other clinical teaching strategies. Assists students in the application of the nursing process to include assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of care. Understands and practices the difference between “doing it for” the student and “supporting the student” during the learning experience. Assists students in the identification of individual learning needs. Promotes, provides, and maintains a safe learning experience. Incorporates student and self as an integral part of the nursing team in the provision of safe patient care when teaching in a simulated environment. Works closely with Supervisor, Lab Faculty to appropriately integrate lab operations, obtain maximum utilization for the most efficient expenditure, and to moderate student and program costs. Support quality improvement measurements related to faculty and student satisfaction. Provides orientation and substantial first cohort support to new Learning Lab Instructors and Simulation Technicians during onboarding to the WGU model and standards for lab instruction. Assist in planning staff schedules. Assist in maintaining the supply inventory. Performs other related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skill and Abilities: Problem solving skills – Investigates appropriate resources and involves partners when appropriate. Is future oriented. Assesses what will help or hinder achieving goals. Focuses on what is important. Interpersonal skills – Deals with others in a considerate, respectful, and unbiased manner. Approaches conflict proactively. Solicits and shares feedback openly. Listens with empathy and maintains composure. Accuracy – Draws on facts collected from a broad knowledge of WGUs goals and processes. Adaptability – Corrects behaviors and communication style to meet the needs of a wide range of situations. Tackle obstacles appropriately and is comfortable with ambiguity. Reliability – Accountable to others; does what it takes to get the job done. Actions are consistent with words. Follows through on commitments. Exhibits exceptional integrity. Attitude – Displays commitment to the organization and to personal growth. Is self-motivated and able to motivate and inspire others. Asserts self appropriately to champion ideas. Tells the truth in a direct and constructive manner. Initiative – Self-directs with a strong tendency for action. Leads the way to improve performance or processes. Displays keen interest in students and organization. Job Qualifications: Minimum Requirements: MSN required (contingent on State Board of Nursing regulations). 2+ years of professional work experience. This individual is a demonstrated subject matter expert with assigned content or practice area(s). Requires an active and unencumbered (will be verified) RN License in the State of the lab location. Preferred Qualifications: Strong experience with distance education and distance learning students is preferred. Experience in simulation-based education is preferred. Experience with integrated technology systems and tools Physical Requirements: Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Must be able to lift up to 15 pounds at times. Working Conditions: This is an on-site only role . Flexibility in working with changing groups of students in a variety of locales. Additional Information Part-Time Intermittent Positions (classified as intermittent and less than 30 standard weekly hours): This is a part-time, intermittent position (classified to work less than 30 SWH) that may be eligible for mental healthcare; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; and prorated paid holidays and accrued sick time. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/full-time-instructor-prelicensure-multiple-specialty-opportunities/job/P1-6652646-0": {
      "title": "Full-Time Instructor, Prelicensure (Multiple Specialty Opportunities)",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Full-Time Instructor, Prelicensure (Multiple Specialty Opportunities) Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Full-Time Instructor, Prelicensure (Multiple Specialty Opportunities) Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-026090 Share this Job United States Remote Posting Date: 09/03/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $73,500.00 - $110,200.00 Western Governors University is currently recruiting for multiple Prelicensure Nursing Instructor opportunities in the following specialty areas: D449 – Psychiatric and Mental Health Nursing D449 – Maternal Psych D447 – Women’s and Children’s Nursing Candidates may be considered for one or more current openings based on their subject-matter expertise and overall qualifications. Applicants are not required to have experience in all three specialty areas. Job Duties Instructors are subject-matter experts who teach and support a caseload of students enrolled in their assigned course(s). Instructors offer specialized instruction on topics within their course(s), aligned with best practices, while monitoring and supporting student progress in competency development and course completion. Instructors are responsive to learner needs and vary the type, length, method, and intensity of instruction to best match each learner’s strengths and goals. Using technology, instructors may interact with students in both group and one-to-one settings. Instructors also collaborate with other instructional and program faculty serving students in their course(s) to ensure continuity and quality of support. Key responsibilities include: Develops instructional materials aligned with identified learning objectives, course competencies, and instructional interventions to support both student self-service use and virtual one-to-many events. Provides effective, relevant, and engaging one-to-many virtual events aligned with identified learning objectives. Continually develops knowledge, skills, and expertise through active participation in faculty learning communities and other professional development opportunities. Provides proactive, relevant, timely, and effective one-to-one virtual instruction to students within a specific course or domain. Facilitates student communities to support peer collaboration, effective faculty interaction, and student development. Provides student-centered, effective one-to-one virtual coaching to help students achieve personal, academic, and career goals. Adapts instructional and coaching practices to meet common and individual student needs. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Subject-matter expertise in the assigned content and skills of the course(s) or domain(s). Strong knowledge of how student characteristics interact with different learning needs common to the assigned course(s) or domain(s). Strong communication skills with the ability to moderate online student communities to encourage engagement and learning. Ability to use information from student profiles, learning behaviors, and interactions to identify individual student needs. Demonstrates respect for and values diverse perspectives and experiences. Ability to adapt standard resources, templates, and instructional plans to meet the needs of individual students or groups of students. Ability to apply adult learning principles and instructional skills to build student competency in a virtual one-to-one setting. Ability to encourage student self-reflection and metacognition to improve competency in learning objectives. Flexibility to adjust instructional approaches based on individual student needs and preferences. Skilled in using data to identify students who may benefit from proactive support and selecting the appropriate tone and content for outreach. Ability to adapt the timing, modality, and frequency of outreach and contact to individual student needs and preferences. Strong active listening skills and emotional intelligence, with the ability to build relationships with adult students. Solid understanding of coaching strategies that support the personal, academic, and professional development of adult students. Willingness to engage in regular self-reflection and reevaluation of beliefs, perspectives, and approaches to improve equity. Proficient in developing presentation materials that align with specified objectives and are visually engaging, understandable, and accessible. Ability to develop learning facilitation experiences and effective formative self-assessment activities aligned with specific objectives to advance student learning. Skilled in implementing relationship-building activities for online student communities. Ability to facilitate synchronous student interaction in a virtual environment. Core Minimum Requirements All candidates must meet the following minimum qualifications: Advanced degree in Nursing and all applicable licenses or certifications. Active, unencumbered compact/multistate RN licensure, with the ability to secure active, unencumbered licensure in all states as required for the role. Three years of highly successful academic practice, based on student outcomes, working with Prelicensure or Undergraduate Nursing students, including at least one year of online faculty experience. Recent clinical or teaching experience within the applicable specialty area within the past five years. Availability to work a student-centered schedule, including evenings and weekends. Ability to travel up to 20% for the role, including required attendance at designated company Summits. Additional travel may be assigned as needed to support business requirements. Specialty Requirements Candidates must demonstrate subject-matter expertise in at least one of the following specialty areas. D449 – Psychiatric and Mental Health Nursing Demonstrated subject-matter expertise in Psychiatric and Mental Health Nursing . D449 – Maternal Psych Demonstrated subject-matter expertise in Psychiatric and Mental Health Nursing . Subject-matter expertise or relevant experience in Women’s and Children’s Nursing is preferred. Candidates with experience spanning psychiatric or mental health nursing and maternal, perinatal, women’s health, postpartum, or related nursing specialties may be particularly well aligned with this opportunity. D447 – Women’s and Children’s Nursing Demonstrated subject-matter expertise in Women’s and Children’s Nursing . Availability to work evenings and weekends, including at least a four-hour scheduled block on Sunday evenings. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree and all applicable domain-specific licenses or certifications. Strong experience with distance education and working with distance-learning students. Demonstrated subject-matter expertise across more than one applicable nursing specialty. Experience teaching across multiple Prelicensure or Undergraduate Nursing courses. Consideration Across Multiple Openings This posting supports multiple active Prelicensure Nursing Instructor openings. Candidates will be evaluated based on their education, licensure, academic experience, recent clinical or teaching experience, schedule availability, and demonstrated subject-matter expertise to determine which current opening or openings best align with their qualifications. Candidates whose backgrounds span multiple specialty areas may be considered for more than one role. Travel Requirements This position requires occasional travel of up to 20%. Required travel includes attendance at designated company Summits, typically one to two times per year. Additional travel may include conferences, visits to company locations, and other business-related events as needed. Additional travel may be assigned based on business requirements. Job Description Disclaimer This position description outlines the major duties, responsibilities, requirements, and working conditions associated with the applicable Prelicensure Nursing Instructor opportunities. It is intended to accurately reflect the current roles; however, management reserves the right to revise or modify requirements as necessary to meet organizational needs. Additional responsibilities may be assigned as circumstances require. Additional Information Full-Time Regular Positions (classified as regular and working 40 standard weekly hours): This is a full-time, regular position (classified for 40 standard weekly hours) that is eligible for bonuses; medical, dental, vision, telehealth and mental healthcare; health savings account and flexible spending account; basic and voluntary life insurance; disability coverage; accident, critical illness and hospital indemnity supplemental coverages; legal and identity theft coverage; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; discounted WGU tuition; and flexible paid time off for rest and relaxation with no need for accrual, flexible paid sick time with no need for accrual, 11 paid holidays, and other paid leaves, including up to 12 weeks of parental leave. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/onsite-instructor-prelicensure-clinical-clinton-mo-part-time/job/P1-6643078-0": {
      "title": "Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Clinton, MO - Part Time Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Clinton, MO - Part Time Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-026071 Share this Job 801 E Sedalia Ave, CLINTON MO, United States Posting Date: 09/02/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $38.79 - $58.17 ***This is an ON-SITE position in the Clinton, MO region*** Prelicensure Clinical Instructors (Hourly) are subject matter experts who teach and mentor students when engaged in experiential clinical course work; in a remote/onsite environment. This faculty position varies in the type, length, and intensity of instructional methods and is based upon student and facility needs. The Clinical Instructor works on a team to support an assigned group of students and offers specialized instruction on challenging experiential/clinical course work. Faculty interacts with students in both group and one-on-one settings. The Clinical Instructor ensures students are successful within their clinical placement setting as they oversee clinical learning. Compensation Expectations: This role is paid hourly and bi-weekly.  The employee will be required to enter all hours worked in an accurate and timely manner. Essential Functions and Responsibilities: Act as a steward for carrying out WGU’s mission and strategic vision.  This faculty must: Demonstrate a high level of commitment, effectiveness, and consistency. Serves as a professional role model for students in communication, ethical comportment, and problem-solving. Provides expertise in an assigned content area and maintains current knowledge in their field. Demonstrates an understanding of, and participates in, the implementation of the philosophy and goals of the program. Fosters students learning through innovative teaching practices; to include how to perform duties in the clinical setting. Responds with urgency to meet student needs and communicates professionally and respectfully with students and all other members of the WGU community. Makes appropriate student referrals for remediation or other needs, utilizing WGU policies and procedures. Communicates with the student's assigned coach/preceptor as needed to discuss student progress and concerns. Provide final review and approval for student's clinical time. Offers proactive support and outreach to assigned students. Uses technology-based teaching and communication platforms to aid students in the development of competencies. Submits electronic clinical student evaluation form(s) after completion of clinical intensive. Collaborates with other professionals within the university to promote a positive, student-obsessed atmosphere. Responsible for responding with urgency to changing requirements, priorities, and short deadlines. Maintains a working knowledge and understanding of relevant state regulations. Conducts both in-person and/remote methods of student evaluation Knowledge, Skill and Abilities: Must be able to work well under stress and meet deadlines. Capacity for self-motivation and working independently. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Aptitude for learning innovative technology. Must comply with site specific orientation and onboarding requirements. Problem Solving Skills: Investigates appropriate resources and involves partners when appropriate; future-oriented; assesses what will help/hinder achieving goals; focuses on what is important. Interpersonal Skills: Deals with others in a considerate, respectful, and unbiased manner; approaches conflict proactively; solicits and shares feedback openly; listens with empathy and maintains composure. Accuracy: Draws on information garnered from careful cultivation of a broad knowledge of WGU’s goals and processes; investigates beyond assumptions. Adaptability: Course corrects behaviors and communication style to meet the needs of a wide range of situations; tackles obstacles appropriately; is comfortable with ambiguity. Reliability: Accountable to others; does what it takes to get the job done; actions are consistent with words; follows through on commitments; exhibits exceptional integrity. Attitude: Displays commitment to the organization and to personal growth; self-motivated and able to motivate and inspire others; asserts self appropriately to champion ideas; tells the truth in a direct and constructive manner. Initiative: Self-directs with a strong bias for action; leads the way in improvement of performance or processes; displays keen interest in students and organization. Competencies: Organizational or Student Impact: Accountable for decisions that impact individual students. Facilitates learning experiences that support student's attainment of knowledge and skills. Acts independently in executing teaching practice with specific guidance from senior faculty and program leaders. Problem Solving & Decision Making: Works on diverse matters of various levels of complexity. Receives general direction from their immediate supervisor or manager. Able to effectively utilize resources to address student concerns and inquiries. Supports students' needs to help them achieve course or program outcomes at the individual student level. Follows university and department established policies and best practices. Communication & Influence: Communicates with students as appropriate to support student questions and needs. Communicates with fellow faculty members as appropriate within and outside of the department. Expected to provide feedback regarding discipline and practice leadership. Leadership & Talent Management Considered a contributing and collegial team member. Adheres to learning and operational quality guidance and instruction Supports initiatives within specialty. Displays a positive attitude toward change and supports change management practices Job Qualifications: Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in nursing; Education is verified. Two years minimum Nursing experience Work history demonstrating continuous advancement and success in roles requiring creative problem solving and collaboration. Unencumbered RN license Active, unencumbered license in designated state State and federal legislative requirements and college accreditation requirements may apply to maintain the necessary credentialing for this role. Work history demonstrating continuous advancement and success in roles requiring creative problem solving and collaboration. As needed, support the Health Placement Team to secure clinical partnerships. Preferred: Doctorate, or terminal degree in a specific content area. Strong experience with distance education and distance learning students is preferred. Terminal degree and all applicable licenses or certifications. Prior experience in clinical teaching/nursing education. , support the Health Placement Team to secure clinical partnerships. Physical Requirements: Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Must be able to lift up to 15 pounds at times. Specific requirements of the job such as travel and the environment in which the job is performed. Additional Information Part-Time Intermittent Positions (classified as intermittent and less than 30 standard weekly hours): This is a part-time, intermittent position (classified to work less than 30 SWH) that may be eligible for mental healthcare; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; and prorated paid holidays and accrued sick time. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/lead-innovation-manager-nursing-and-health/job/P1-6568609-0": {
      "title": "Site Navigation",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Lead Innovation Manager, Nursing and Health Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Lead Innovation Manager, Nursing and Health Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-025997 Share this Job 4001 South 700 East, Salt Lake City UT, United States Posting Date: 09/02/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $123,000.00 - $190,700.00 The Simulation and Learning Innovation Manager provides strategic leadership for the development, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of simulation-based education and experiential learning opportunities across undergraduate and graduate nursing programs. This role supports WGU’s mission of competency-based, student-centered education by advancing innovative, scalable, and evidence-based simulation and clinical learning experiences . L eads initiatives that integrate emerging simulation technologies, virtual and digital learning strategies, and experiential education best practices to enhance student engagement, clinical judgment, and workforce readiness in online and hybrid learning environments. The position collaborates closely with academic leadership, faculty, clinical partners, and operational teams to ensure alignment with accreditation standards, regulatory requirements, and institutional goals. Responsibilities Primary Responsibilities Strategic Leadership & Program Development Provide strategic leadership for simulation and experiential learning initiatives across undergraduate and graduate nursing and health programs. Develop and implement a long-term vision for simulation and experiential learning aligned with WGU’s mission, strategic priorities, and competency-based education model. Lead innovation in virtual simulation, digital learning technologies, augmented and mixed reality applications, and scalable experiential learning solutions for distributed learners. Establish and maintain standards of excellence in simulation education consistent with national best practices and accreditation requirements, including pursuit and maintenance of relevant simulation accreditation standards. Oversee operational, budgetary, resource allocation, and personnel functions associated with simulation and experiential learning activities. Identify and develop strategic partnerships and external opportunities that support program growth, innovation, and sustainability. Curriculum Integration & Educational Effectiveness Collaborate with academic leadership and faculty to integrate simulation and experiential learning experiences throughout nursing and health program curricula. Support the design, implementation, and evaluation of competency-based simulation experiences that strengthen clinical reasoning, decision-making, teamwork, communication, and patient-centered care. Ensure simulation and experiential learning activities align with accreditation standards, licensure requirements, state board regulations, and program outcomes. Expand and enhance virtual, in-person, and hybrid experiential learning opportunities to support diverse student populations and geographically distributed learners. Promote evidence-based simulation methodologies, debriefing practices, learner assessment strategies, and outcome evaluation processes. Support scalable clinical replacement strategies and experiential learning models that enhance student access and educational quality. Faculty Development & Academic Support Provide leadership, mentorship, and professional development opportunities for faculty engaged in simulation-based and experiential teaching. Support faculty adoption of innovative instructional technologies and simulation pedagogies. Foster a culture of collaboration, innovation, continuous improvement, and evidence-based teaching practices. Encourage and support faculty engagement in simulation research, quality improvement initiatives, and scholarly dissemination. Operations & Technology Management Oversee operational coordination of simulation and experiential learning resources, technologies, and platforms. Ensure effective implementation, maintenance, evaluation, and continuous improvement of simulation technologies and digital learning tools. Develop and maintain policies, procedures, and quality standards supporting simulation and experiential learning activities. Collaborate with university operational and technology teams to optimize learner access, scalability, and user experience across virtual and distributed environments. Monitor trends, emerging technologies, and industry best practices to support innovation and program advancement. Partnerships & External Engagement Establish and strengthen partnerships with healthcare organizations, clinical agencies, professional associations, and community stakeholders to support experiential learning opportunities. Represent WGU in national and regional simulation, nursing education, and healthcare workforce initiatives. Collaborate with external partners to expand innovative experiential learning models and workforce readiness initiatives. Support external funding opportunities, and strategic initiatives that advance simulation and experiential learning programs. Assessment & Continuous Improvement Develop and implement assessment and quality improvement strategies to evaluate the effectiveness and outcomes of simulation and experiential learning initiatives. Analyze program outcomes, student performance data, and stakeholder feedback to guide continuous improvement efforts. Lead and support research and scholarly activity related to simulation education, competency-based learning, and experiential education innovation. Disseminate findings through presentations, publications, professional organizations, and collaborative partnerships. Promote data-informed decision-making and evidence-based educational practices across simulation and experiential learning initiatives. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. This job description includes a general representation of job requirements rather than a comprehensive inventory of all required responsibilities or work activities . The contents of this document or related job requirements may change at any time with or without notice. Qualifications Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Expertise in simulation-based and competency-based nursing and health education, including curriculum design, learner assessment, and student-centered instructional strategies. Strong knowledge of nursing and health program accreditation, licensure, regulatory standards, and experiential learning compliance requirements. Proficiency in healthcare technologies, virtual simulation platforms, learning management systems, and emerging educational innovations. Experience with quality improvement, program evaluation, data analysis, and evidence-based continuous improvement initiatives. Skilled in faculty development, adult learning principles, mentoring, and supporting adoption of innovative teaching practices. Demonstrated leadership, strategic planning, operational management, budgeting, and organizational development expertise . Excellent communication, facilitation, presentation, and stakeholder engagement skills across academic, healthcare, and executive environments. Strong collaboration and relationship-building abilities with cross-functional, distributed, and external partner teams. Effective project management, problem-solving, and decision-making skills in fast-paced, evolving environments. Proven ability to lead organizational change, foster inclusive and student-centered cultures, and support scalable educational models for diverse learners. Minimum Qualifications Education Master's degree i n relevant area from an accredited institution . Experience Minimum of five (5) years of academic leadership, teaching, simulation, or experiential learning experience in nursing and health education. Demonstrated experience in curriculum development, simulation integration, and competency-based education. Experience leading complex projects, operational initiatives, or interdisciplinary teams in academic or healthcare environments. Knowledge of nursing and health accreditation standards, licensure requirements, and regulatory expectations related to simulation and clinical education. Experience using learning technologies, virtual simulation platforms, and digital education tools. Strong written, verbal, organizational, and interpersonal communication skills . Preferred Qualifications Doctorate degree in relevant area from an accredited institution Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator (CHSE) or other relevant simulation certification . Experience in online, hybrid, or competency-based education models. Experience with Society for Simulation in Healthcare (SSH) accreditation processes or simulation program standards. Demonstrated success in faculty development, mentoring, and change management initiatives. Experience managing budgets, operational planning, and resource allocation. Experience developing partnerships with healthcare organizations, workforce partners, or community stakeholders. Experience leading innovation initiatives involving virtual reality (VR), augmented reality (AR), mixed reality (MR), or emerging educational technologies Physical Requirements: Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Must be able to lift up to 15 pounds at times. Working Condition: This position requires occasional travel of up to 20%, including required attendance at designated company summits (typically one to two per year). Additional travel may include conferences, visits to company locations, and other business-related events as needed. Additional travel may be assigned as needed to support business requirements. #LI-TT1  #LI-INOFFICE Additional Information Full-Time Regular Positions (classified as regular and working 40 standard weekly hours): This is a full-time, regular position (classified for 40 standard weekly hours) that is eligible for bonuses; medical, dental, vision, telehealth and mental healthcare; health savings account and flexible spending account; basic and voluntary life insurance; disability coverage; accident, critical illness and hospital indemnity supplemental coverages; legal and identity theft coverage; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; discounted WGU tuition; and flexible paid time off for rest and relaxation with no need for accrual, flexible paid sick time with no need for accrual, 11 paid holidays, and other paid leaves, including up to 12 weeks of parental leave. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/remote-visiting-instructor-nutrition-pennsylvania-part-time-temp/job/P1-6261514-0": {
      "title": "Remote Visiting Instructor, Nutrition",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Remote Visiting Instructor, Nutrition - Pennsylvania - Part Time Temp Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Remote Visiting Instructor, Nutrition - Pennsylvania - Part Time Temp Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-025750 Share this Job United States Remote Posting Date: 09/01/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $32.11 - $48.12 ​ ***This is a REMOTE position throughout Pennsylvania. *** The Visiting Instructor provides specialized instruction for courses focusing on concepts for students. Student learning is the primary responsibility of WGU faculty. Visiting Instructors are subject matter experts who teach and support students. Visiting Instructors offer specialized instruction on topics in their course(s) aligned with best practices, as well as monitor and support student progress in competency development. They are responsive to learner needs and vary the type, length, method, and intensity of instruction best matched to the learner’s strengths and goals. Using technology, Visiting Instructors may interact with students in both group and one-on-one settings. Instructors collaborate with other instructional and program faculty serving the students to ensure continuity and quality of support. Essential Functions and Responsibilities: Provide specialized instruction on assigned topics aligned with course curriculum and best practices. Monitor the course progress of an assigned group of learners in their course(s) and proactively offer support at key points of the student journey. Provide expertise in assigned content area and maintains current knowledge in their field. Foster student learning through innovative, effective teaching practices. Use technology-based teaching and communication platforms to aid students in the development of competencies. Collaborate with other professionals within the university to promote a positive, student-obsessed atmosphere. Other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Knowledge, Skill and Abilities: Demonstrated ability to customize instructional support for learners with a variety of needs and educational backgrounds Must demonstrate technological competency: Proficiency in Microsoft Office (or similar) applications, virtual instructional platforms, and student management systems Extraordinary customer service orientation Strong verbal and written communication skills, with ability to present information clearly, concisely, and accurately; friendly, persuasive speaking and writing style Communicate effectively and respectfully within the context of varying beliefs, behaviors, orientations, identities, and cultural backgrounds and situations Well organized - conscientious and detail-oriented Adapt to changing priorities within the workplace Demonstrate initiative through independent completion of tasks Ability to use data to make decisions Strong understanding, acceptance, adherence, and promotion of the tenets of competency-based education in the WGU model Minimum Qualifications: Must maintain an active and unencumbered Registered Dietitian (RD) or Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) license to practice dietetics-nutrition in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Master’s degree in Nutrition and Dietetics/Nutritional Science, or Public Health in Nutrition, or Dietetics Administration. Education must be from an accredited institution. Education is verified. Higher education experience providing instruction support for 2 years. Industry experience for a minimum of 2 years. This position requires afternoon and evening hours, up to 10 hours a week. This position requires occasional travel of up to 20%, including required attendance at designated company summits (typically one to two per year). Additional travel may include conferences, visits to company locations, and other business-related events as needed. Additional travel may be assigned as needed to support business requirements. Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate or terminal degree in content area. Education must be from an accredited institution. Education is verified. Experience with distance education and distance learning students. Physical Requirements: Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Works primarily from home within the continental United States and is available to travel to meetings as required. Must be able to lift up to 15 pounds at times. Additional Information Part-Time Intermittent Positions (classified as intermittent and less than 30 standard weekly hours): This is a part-time, intermittent position (classified to work less than 30 SWH) that may be eligible for mental healthcare; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; and prorated paid holidays and accrued sick time. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/academic-careers/page/1": {
      "title": "Course Instructor",
      "description": "Academic & Faculty Careers | WGU Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Academic Careers Educate. Motivate. Transform. Academic careers at WGU focus on supporting learners through mentorship, instruction, and meaningful assessment.\n        As a faculty member or academic leader, you’ll help learners build real-world skills, stay on track, and move\n        confidently toward their goals. Find a Teaching Role That Matches Your Passion for Education Academic Career Paths Faculty Faculty roles at WGU are about making a direct, meaningful difference in learners' lives. You'll serve\n                  as a Mentor, Instructor, or Evaluator, providing personalized support, coaching, and instruction that\n                  helps learners progress with confidence in a flexible, competency-based environment. Accreditation & Compliance Accreditation and Compliance roles support the foundation that makes everything else possible. You'll\n                  help ensure academic quality, integrity, and trust—working behind the scenes to meet regulatory\n                  standards while enabling innovation and a continuous improvement model. Academic Strategy Academic Strategy roles are ideal for big-picture thinkers who enjoy turning insight into action.\n                  You'll work at the intersection of data, innovation, and academic excellence—helping WGU design,\n                  launch, and evolve programs that meet the needs of today's learners and tomorrow's workforce. Academic Leadership Academic Leadership roles are for those who want to lead with purpose and shape the future of\n                  education. In this area, you'll guide academic teams, influence strategy, and help scale innovative\n                  learning models that expand access and improve learner outcomes. Program Development & Learning Design Program Development and Learning Design roles are for creators and problem-solvers who want to build\n                  impactful learning experiences. In this area, you'll collaborate with academic and industry partners\n                  to design modern, engaging programs that prepare learners for real-world success. Program Mentor Our Program Mentors are the heart of our student success model at WGU. As a Program Mentor, you'll have the\n          unique opportunity to provide personalized, one-on-one guidance to students, helping them navigate their\n          educational journey with confidence and success. Hear from our Program Mentors Evaluators Our Evaluators help turn achievement into opportunity. As an Evaluator, you’ll use your expertise to assess student\n          work, provide meaningful feedback, and validate the competencies that move learners forward. If you’re driven by\n          quality, purpose, and helping students succeed, this is where your impact matters. Hear from our Evaluators Course Instructor Our Course Instructors bring learning to life at WGU. As a Course Instructor, you’ll have the opportunity to guide, coach, and inspire students as they build confidence, develop new skills, and progress toward their goals. Through meaningful connections and expert support, you’ll help turn potential into progress and make a lasting impact along the way. Hear from our Course Instructors Subject Matter Experts Our Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) help shape the learning experiences that power student success at WGU. As a recognized\n          expert in your field, you'll contribute as an independent contractor (1099), partnering with academic and learning\n          design teams on project-based work to create relevant, engaging course content that reflects current industry practices\n          and workforce needs. Through your expertise, you'll help ensure learners gain the knowledge and skills needed to achieve\n          their goals. View SME Opportunities Hear from Our People \"I absolutely love my role because it allows me to support students at some of the most pivotal moments in\n              their academic and professional journeys. As a Senior Program Mentor, my 'why' is rooted in helping\n              students build confidence, navigate challenges, and realize they are capable of far more than they\n              initially believed, just like my WGU Program Mentor did for me. This job feels like 'paying it forward'\n              and building meaningful connections all at the same time. Watching students overcome obstacles, persist\n              toward their goals, and grow throughout their program is what makes this work deeply meaningful to me.\" Lauren C., Sr. Program Mentor \"What I love most about my role is helping students realize that they can earn their education on their\n              own terms and that success is possible, even when life is complex. As a two-time WGU graduate, I bring\n              both lived experience and practical insight into my mentoring, using what I've learned to better support\n              students as they work toward their goals. What keeps me invested is WGU's innovative spirit and genuine\n              willingness to listen. Ideas are encouraged, growth is supported, and improving the student experience is\n              a shared responsibility. I've built a career here that I'm deeply proud of, and that pride shows up in the\n              care, consistency, and quality of support I provide to every student I serve.\" Wesley R., Sr. Program Mentor \"I've spent most of my life working in Education and Mental Health. As a Program Mentor, I get to use a\n              unique blend of both skillsets to help students navigate their academic, professional, and personal lives.\n              Each student's story is different; it's my role to truly listen, support, and meet each student where\n              they're at every single day.\" Ryan S., Program Mentor Get Answers and Take the Next Step Sage can answer questions, help you explore roles, and guide you through applying at WGU, right when you\n          need it. Chat now Open Jobs I'm Looking For Positions Near Use your location Search Search filters Filter Results Job Category Academic Affairs 1 Academic Community of Care 20 Administrative Community of Care 2 Program Development 9 City Albuquerque 1 ALEXANDRIA 1 CLINTON 1 College Station 1 DALLAS 1 DAYTONA 1 EL PASO 2 Elko 2 FORT WAYNE 1 State Florida 1 Indiana 2 Missouri 3 Nevada 3 New Mexico 1 Texas 7 Utah 14 Virginia 1 Clear Filter Showing 1 - 10 of 32 jobs Sort By Date Date Job Title Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - College Station, TX - Part Time Job Location College Station, TX College Station, TX Posting Date: 09/08/2026 JR-026106 PART_TIME Apply Now Associate Instructional Technologist Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/08/2026 JR-026104 FULL_TIME Apply Now Operations Manager Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/08/2026 JR-026097 FULL_TIME Apply Now Associate Instructional Designer Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/08/2026 JR-026072 FULL_TIME Apply Now Program Development Owner Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/08/2026 JR-024806 FULL_TIME Apply Now Senior Staff Attorney Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/08/2026 JR-025567 FULL_TIME Apply Now Academic Initiatives Strategist Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/08/2026 JR-026092 FULL_TIME Apply Now Senior Strategist - Future of Education and AI Innovation Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/04/2026 JR-026100 FULL_TIME Apply Now Senior Psychometrician Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-025820 FULL_TIME Apply Now Full-Time Student Records Specialist - On-Site WGU Campus - Salt Lake City Location Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-026008 FULL_TIME Apply Now Go to first page Go to previous page 1 2 3 4 Go to next page Go to last page 10 20 Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/academic-careers/page/2": {
      "title": "Course Instructor",
      "description": "Academic & Faculty Careers | WGU Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Academic Careers Educate. Motivate. Transform. Academic careers at WGU focus on supporting learners through mentorship, instruction, and meaningful assessment.\n        As a faculty member or academic leader, you’ll help learners build real-world skills, stay on track, and move\n        confidently toward their goals. Find a Teaching Role That Matches Your Passion for Education Academic Career Paths Faculty Faculty roles at WGU are about making a direct, meaningful difference in learners' lives. You'll serve\n                  as a Mentor, Instructor, or Evaluator, providing personalized support, coaching, and instruction that\n                  helps learners progress with confidence in a flexible, competency-based environment. Accreditation & Compliance Accreditation and Compliance roles support the foundation that makes everything else possible. You'll\n                  help ensure academic quality, integrity, and trust—working behind the scenes to meet regulatory\n                  standards while enabling innovation and a continuous improvement model. Academic Strategy Academic Strategy roles are ideal for big-picture thinkers who enjoy turning insight into action.\n                  You'll work at the intersection of data, innovation, and academic excellence—helping WGU design,\n                  launch, and evolve programs that meet the needs of today's learners and tomorrow's workforce. Academic Leadership Academic Leadership roles are for those who want to lead with purpose and shape the future of\n                  education. In this area, you'll guide academic teams, influence strategy, and help scale innovative\n                  learning models that expand access and improve learner outcomes. Program Development & Learning Design Program Development and Learning Design roles are for creators and problem-solvers who want to build\n                  impactful learning experiences. In this area, you'll collaborate with academic and industry partners\n                  to design modern, engaging programs that prepare learners for real-world success. Program Mentor Our Program Mentors are the heart of our student success model at WGU. As a Program Mentor, you'll have the\n          unique opportunity to provide personalized, one-on-one guidance to students, helping them navigate their\n          educational journey with confidence and success. Hear from our Program Mentors Evaluators Our Evaluators help turn achievement into opportunity. As an Evaluator, you’ll use your expertise to assess student\n          work, provide meaningful feedback, and validate the competencies that move learners forward. If you’re driven by\n          quality, purpose, and helping students succeed, this is where your impact matters. Hear from our Evaluators Course Instructor Our Course Instructors bring learning to life at WGU. As a Course Instructor, you’ll have the opportunity to guide, coach, and inspire students as they build confidence, develop new skills, and progress toward their goals. Through meaningful connections and expert support, you’ll help turn potential into progress and make a lasting impact along the way. Hear from our Course Instructors Subject Matter Experts Our Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) help shape the learning experiences that power student success at WGU. As a recognized\n          expert in your field, you'll contribute as an independent contractor (1099), partnering with academic and learning\n          design teams on project-based work to create relevant, engaging course content that reflects current industry practices\n          and workforce needs. Through your expertise, you'll help ensure learners gain the knowledge and skills needed to achieve\n          their goals. View SME Opportunities Hear from Our People \"I absolutely love my role because it allows me to support students at some of the most pivotal moments in\n              their academic and professional journeys. As a Senior Program Mentor, my 'why' is rooted in helping\n              students build confidence, navigate challenges, and realize they are capable of far more than they\n              initially believed, just like my WGU Program Mentor did for me. This job feels like 'paying it forward'\n              and building meaningful connections all at the same time. Watching students overcome obstacles, persist\n              toward their goals, and grow throughout their program is what makes this work deeply meaningful to me.\" Lauren C., Sr. Program Mentor \"What I love most about my role is helping students realize that they can earn their education on their\n              own terms and that success is possible, even when life is complex. As a two-time WGU graduate, I bring\n              both lived experience and practical insight into my mentoring, using what I've learned to better support\n              students as they work toward their goals. What keeps me invested is WGU's innovative spirit and genuine\n              willingness to listen. Ideas are encouraged, growth is supported, and improving the student experience is\n              a shared responsibility. I've built a career here that I'm deeply proud of, and that pride shows up in the\n              care, consistency, and quality of support I provide to every student I serve.\" Wesley R., Sr. Program Mentor \"I've spent most of my life working in Education and Mental Health. As a Program Mentor, I get to use a\n              unique blend of both skillsets to help students navigate their academic, professional, and personal lives.\n              Each student's story is different; it's my role to truly listen, support, and meet each student where\n              they're at every single day.\" Ryan S., Program Mentor Get Answers and Take the Next Step Sage can answer questions, help you explore roles, and guide you through applying at WGU, right when you\n          need it. Chat now Open Jobs I'm Looking For Positions Near Use your location Search Search filters Filter Results Job Category Academic Affairs 1 Academic Community of Care 20 Administrative Community of Care 2 Program Development 9 City Albuquerque 1 ALEXANDRIA 1 CLINTON 1 College Station 1 DALLAS 1 DAYTONA 1 EL PASO 2 Elko 2 FORT WAYNE 1 State Florida 1 Indiana 2 Missouri 3 Nevada 3 New Mexico 1 Texas 7 Utah 14 Virginia 1 Clear Filter Showing 11 - 20 of 32 jobs Sort By Date Date Job Title Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Houston, TX - Full Time Job Location Houston, TX Houston, TX Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-025338 FULL_TIME Apply Now Onsite Instructor, Learning Lab - Indianapolis, IN - Part Time Job Location Indianapolis, IN Indianapolis, IN Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-026079 PART_TIME Apply Now Full-Time Instructor, Prelicensure (Multiple Specialty Opportunities) Job Location Salt Lake City, UT + 1 More Locations United States Remote Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-026090 FULL_TIME Apply Now Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Clinton, MO - Part Time Job Location CLINTON, MO Clinton, MO Posting Date: 09/02/2026 JR-026071 PART_TIME Apply Now Lead Innovation Manager, Nursing and Health Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/02/2026 JR-025997 FULL_TIME Apply Now Remote Visiting Instructor, Nutrition - Pennsylvania - Part Time Temp Job Location Salt Lake City, UT + 1 More Locations United States Remote Posting Date: 09/01/2026 JR-025750 PART_TIME Apply Now Assessment Developer Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 08/27/2026 JR-024398 FULL_TIME Apply Now Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Alexandria, VA - Part Time Job Location ALEXANDRIA, VA Alexandria, VA Posting Date: 08/25/2026 JR-025920 PART_TIME Apply Now Assessment Strategist Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 08/25/2026 JR-025166 FULL_TIME Apply Now Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Fort Wayne, IN - Part Time Job Location FORT WAYNE, IN Fort Wayne, IN Posting Date: 08/25/2026 JR-025686 PART_TIME Apply Now Go to first page Go to previous page 1 2 3 4 Go to next page Go to last page 10 20 Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
